# UI + Architecture

## Common widgets
Build once in `lib/common/`, reuse everywhere. Extend via props — never duplicate.
Create components only when needed (buttons, fields, AuroraBackground, cards, snackbars, loaders, StatusBadge, LanguageSelector, etc.).

## Design system (`lib/core/`)
Centralize: colors, spacing, radius, typography, theme, shadows, dimensions.
No hardcoded repeated colors/spacing/type styles. Keep Aurora header consistent on Splash/Welcome/Login/Register/OTP.

## MVVM
View = UI only. ViewModel = state/presentation. Repository = data. Service = API. Model = types.
No API calls or business logic in widgets. Use Riverpod.

## Folders
Flutter: `app` `core` `common` `data` `features` `l10n`
Backend: `config` `common` `middleware` `modules` `providers` `database`
No unnecessary nesting.
